{"connection_id": "BC-4515cccc7e19967de0cc", "ref": "WLC:Deut.30.19", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "choosing life rather than death", "note": "Moses sets life and death, blessing and curse before Israel and calls for choosing life. It provides covenantal language for the commentary's opposed outcomes of a shown way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-55f1348aeb1e834815fd", "ref": "WLC:Deut.32.13", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "riding on the heights of the land", "note": "God makes Israel ride on the heights of the land. It is a poetic counterpart to the commentary's mount and elevated ridge, though it does not itself explain the ease of ascent."}
