{"connection_id": "BC-2b2f8b88d536fdc8d449", "ref": "WLC:Isa.28.16", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith without hurrying", "note": "The commentary's good hedy is not a fleeing rush. Isaiah says the one who trusts will not act in haste, giving calm movement a faith-based interpretation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-adc71731d3bb9071f1b9", "ref": "WLC:Isa.30.21", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "a voice behind says, “This is the way”", "note": "The commentary calls the guide one who goes ahead; Isaiah’s traveler hears a voice behind identifying the way to walk, a concrete reversal of the guide’s position while preserving the path instruction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a3623c355381fa605ab9", "ref": "WLC:Isa.30.21", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "this is the way", "note": "When a traveler turns right or left, Isaiah's voice says, \"This is the way; walk in it.\" That is a precise counterpart to the commentary's guide who identifies a road rather than merely giving advice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-919eee22f68541416e83", "ref": "WLC:Isa.30.22", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "casting away images", "note": "The commentary contrasts the wretched person who keeps the reminder at a distance with Abraham's request to be kept from idols. Isaiah commands defiling and casting away idol-images as something unclean."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b706c3b47cac8037ce52", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "strengthen weak hands and feeble knees", "note": "The commentary’s secondary walking image is a weak person relying on support; Isaiah tells the hearers to strengthen weak hands and make firm feeble knees, a concrete bodily response to weakness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-41df7009f656d57d31c7", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.3", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "strengthen weak hands and feeble knees", "note": "The commentary's secondary h-d-y image is a weakened person needing support. Isaiah commands the strengthening of weak hands and unsteady knees before its highway vision."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fb1740f219d15ca2f9b8", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the lame leap like a deer", "note": "The commentary links a mount’s light legs with a ridge that can be climbed; Isaiah says the lame will leap like a deer, turning impaired gait into agile movement."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5bee0f6c5207d0be4c29", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.6", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lame person leaping like a deer", "note": "Isaiah's lame person leaps like a deer. This is a sharply specific transformation of weak legs into the light, high-country movement developed in the commentary."}
{"connection_id": "BC-178262e591d6e69981c0", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "a highway on which even a fool will not stray", "note": "The commentary describes being made ready for the easier way; Isaiah’s holy highway is so clearly marked that even a fool will not err on it, a concrete image of an accessible route."}
{"connection_id": "BC-31b3a9fc113d6029f815", "ref": "WLC:Isa.35.8", "target": "sec14", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "highway on which travelers do not stray", "note": "Isaiah's holy highway is a route on which even inexperienced travelers do not go astray. It joins the commentary's explicit guiding with a road made reliable for its walkers."}

